grammar: ./parser.mly

This tool tunes one thing: the grammar's %on_error_reduce list. For
each construct on that list, when the parse fails just after the
construct is complete, its error message reads "Assuming that the
<construct> is complete, expecting ..." instead of listing everything
the construct itself could have continued with. Adding a construct to
the list trades a plain "Expecting ..." list for that "Assuming ..."
phrasing; removing one does the reverse.

on the list now (3): block expr list(stmt)

### CALIBRATION: replay the recorded keep/remove decisions
  (removing a kept construct, or re-adding a removed one, must score non-improving)
  agreement: 2 / 2

